      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A statistical model for the incomplete diallel with reciprocals was first proposed by Yates (1947). Under this design, all $ N \\times N $ crosses are employed, except those on the diagonals (Figure 20.2, center). As in the case of Design II with reciprocals, this type of diallel yields reciprocal full and half sibs, in addition to paternal half-sib, maternal half-sib, and full-sib families, providing an opportunity to estimate variance components beyond those possible in a design without",
