      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "reciprocals. Our description will be in terms of the Cockerham-Weir (1977b) model, Equation 20.6a, described above in the context of Design II. The analysis of variance, given in Table 20.5, contains mean squares for reciprocal general (RGCA) and specific (RSCA) combining abilities, in addition to the GCA and SCA terms just described. These are functions of the five causal components of genetic variance associated with the Cockerham-Weir model (see Table 20.5).",
