    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "With this design, the variances associated with maternal and paternal extranuclear effects, $ \\sigma_{m}^{2} $ and $ \\sigma_{p}^{2} $, always appear together as a sum in the expected mean squares, so the method of moments cannot generate separate estimates of them. To accomplish that, Cockerham and Weir (1977b) proposed the use of the symmetrical products,",
