    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The difference $ T_{m} - T_{p} $ provides an estimate of $ \\sigma_{m}^{2} - \\sigma_{p}^{2} $, which when combined with the estimate of $ (\\sigma_{m}^{2} + \\sigma_{p}^{2}) $ obtained from the analysis of variance, allows the separation of $ \\sigma_{m}^{2} $ and $ \\sigma_{p}^{2} $.",
